      soWhat: 'On a real arm, one episode is one attempt at the task, for example one drawing pass: tens of seconds. You cannot afford thousands of noisy episodes. Every change that removes noise from the push (credit after the action, a baseline, a critic) saves real arm time.',
      cannotTeach: 'CartPole gives a reward at every step. A robot task that is scored only at the end has no "rewards after the action" to separate. See the level "Pass or fail".',
